=== D-205: the class root cause, stated once ===
    D-197, D-201 and D-205 are one class. Each guard asked a
    NARROWER question than the harm it names:

      defect       the question it asked              the harm it names
      D-197/D-201  is this suffix in a table          does a reader OPEN this name
      D-200        is the strip symmetric             did the command EMIT this
      D-205        is the capture's run a suffix      is every discarded line HEADER

    the principle, pinned in evidence.py:
      a guard that discards, skips or exempts input must PROVE
      each discarded unit against the rule that names the
      exemption; anything not proven is subject to the check.

=== the header grammar — what may be discarded, and nothing else ===
    known directives : cmd, for, timeout, volatile
    header           : contiguous leading '# evidence-<known>:' lines
                       plus ONE blank separator
    everything else  : BODY — '#'-prefixed or not — compared
                       byte for byte against the capture

=== the three runs that differ by one character ===
    A  honest log                              accepted
    B  the same log, claim prefixed with '#'   REFUSED
    C  control: the same claim, no '#'         REFUSED
    B and C differ by ONE character. At cb77e83, B was
    ACCEPTED at both doors: Foundry-Accept-Casting reported an
    accepted evidence verdict, and Foundry-Phase(inspect_start)
    reported mismatches [] and advanced the cycle counter.

=== the second accepted shape the defect named ===
    a forged '#' line ABOVE a capture whose own output
    legitimately begins with '#' lines, where the capture's
    run is still a suffix of the committed one:
      REFUSED, and the diff names the forged line:
        -# FORGED: the guard holds on every path

=== the true accepts the narrowing keeps ===
    honest capture beginning with '#' lines (D-198's subject)  accepted
    cat-replay: the capture IS the whole committed file        accepted
    two blank lines written; the command emits the second      accepted

=== the smuggling shape the KNOWN-directive set closes ===
    '# evidence-summary:' is not a directive the parser reads,
    so it is body, and a command that never printed it is
    REFUSED. A grammar of 'any # evidence-*: shape' would have
    discarded it unread — the same hole, one notch narrower.

